WEBVTT

00:06:56.863 --> 00:07:00.084
DC: I mean, I also
wouldn't have hired me either,

00:07:00.108 --> 00:07:01.299
to be honest.

00:07:01.323 --> 00:07:04.757
And maybe that's a reason
why people aren't honest,

00:07:04.781 --> 00:07:08.291
is because they feel they have to be
a different version of themselves.

00:07:09.029 --> 00:07:10.762
AG: If you're a skilled interviewer,

00:07:10.786 --> 00:07:12.715
you know you can get around that problem

00:07:12.739 --> 00:07:14.707
by testing people's knowledge and skills.

00:07:14.731 --> 00:07:16.961
But many interviewers
don't even know what kind

00:07:16.985 --> 00:07:19.064
of knowledge and skills
they're looking for.

00:07:19.088 --> 00:07:20.374
So they ask brain teasers,

00:07:20.398 --> 00:07:24.775
like, "How many paperclips
would fill Yankee Stadium,"

00:07:24.799 --> 00:07:27.459
or "How many elevators
are there in America?"

00:07:27.483 --> 00:07:29.014
DC: Because I can't answer that,

00:07:29.038 --> 00:07:30.991
doesn't mean that I won't be successful.